{
  "//": [
    "Q06 — A customer's purchase streaks",
    "What it answers: \"What were this customer's longest runs of buying something on consecutive days?\"",
    "Route:           GET /customers/streaks   (params: customer_id; every route also takes db=)",
    "Pattern:         gaps_and_islands",
    "Engine:          MongoDB",
    "Think about it:",
    "The same gaps-and-islands idea as SQL, written as pipeline stages: $group,",
    "$setWindowFields, $dateSubtract. Which stage reads the documents, how many",
    "does it read, and is the rest of the pipeline expensive?"
  ],
  "aggregate": "purchases",
  "cursor": {},
  "pipeline": [
    {
      "$match": {
        "customer_id": "{{customer_id}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "$group": {
        "_id": "$purchase_date"
      }
    },
    {
      "$setWindowFields": {
        "sortBy": {
          "_id": 1
        },
        "output": {
          "rn": {
            "$documentNumber": {}
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$group": {
        "_id": {
          "$dateSubtract": {
            "startDate": "$_id",
            "unit": "day",
            "amount": "$rn"
          }
        },
        "streak_start": {
          "$min": "$_id"
        },
        "streak_end": {
          "$max": "$_id"
        },
        "days": {
          "$sum": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$match": {
        "days": {
          "$gte": 2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$sort": {
        "days": -1,
        "streak_start": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "$limit": 10
    },
    {
      "$project": {
        "_id": 0,
        "streak_start": 1,
        "streak_end": 1,
        "days": 1
      }
    }
  ]
}
